A||N||10||Monkeyman||Couple quick questions||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||12-28-2000||08:23 PM||||1st--There doesn't seem to be quite enough clearance between the top (leading edge) of the passenger door and the front fender.  It's already started to rub away some of the paint, etc.  What can I do to fix this?  I don't think it would take much more than about a 1/4 of an inch to take care of the problem.<P>2nd--The drivers side outside mirror has a cracked glass.  Can I just replace the glass or do I have to replace the entire mirror?  If I can get away with just replacing the glass, how do I do it?  I have power mirrors if it matters.||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||12-28-2000||08:29 PM||||MM, any auto glass shop has or can order the<BR>per-cut mirror glass. I did my passs. side<BR>I think it was $15.00. YOU MUST BREAK THE OLD ONE OUT. use silicone on the new glass<BR>(RTV)<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||2
Z||000002||Old Lar||12-28-2000||08:31 PM||||1st: sounds like a fender alignment problem.  Can't you just loosen the fender mounting bolts and shift the fender 1/4 inch.<P>2nd:  the glass alone can be replaced.   I'm not sure how it got done.  I had Bob Steiger replace the glass on my GT with power mirrors.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||12-28-2000||08:32 PM||||There is adjustment at the hinges, just loosen the bolts, don't totally loosen them. And then set your door wher eit needs to be and tighten the bolts.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 12-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||80's BOY||12-28-2000||08:42 PM||||for the door, if you're bushings are worn out then adjustment alone might not be enough. they are cheap, and GM usually has them in stock. i had the exact same problem.||||reg||3
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-28-2000||08:45 PM||||Thanx, guys.  I'll call the glass shop tomorrow and take a look at the hinges sometime this weekend.  Hopefully I can get started on my stereo installation this weekend, too.  I just need my friend to get back to work (currently off sick) so he can make me a rear panel to mount the amp in.  I may have to just rest it behind the passenger seat for now since it may be a while before I can get the panel made and I've just got to get the stereo hooked up and running.  Also have to work on the headlights.<P>That's the next question/problem.  Apparently, the headlights (only one?) won't go down all the way.  Might be a problem with something binding?  Where can I look?  What can I check?  I could simply swap assys with the ones on the Grape Ape, but that seems like alot of trouble if there's something simple I can fix on the GT.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-28-2000||08:48 PM||||80's Boy--Good suggestion, but I doubt it's the bushings.  1st, it's the top of the door that's rubbing, not the bottom (door should sag if the bushings are shot, right?).  Second, there doesn't seem to be any wear on the door sill.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MrPBody||12-28-2000||09:38 PM||||<B>Door:</B> Try to determine if you need to move the door back or the fender forward.  Look at the gap all around the door, and compare it to the driver's side.  See if the door looks like it's tilted up in back.  If you need to adjust the door, then I guess you loosen the hinge bolts as suggested above.  (Whatever your manual says -- I haven't tried this yet.)  To solve this problem on my '85, I moved the fender forward slightly.  To do this, I removed the rocker panel for access to two rivets that retain the fender, removed the fender, and slotted the rearmost upper mounting hole (next to the cowl) as well as the antenna hole.  The other mounting holes are already slotted or oversize.<P><B>Mirror:</B>  I have seen replacement mirror glass at Pep Boys and other auto parts stores.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ronnie||12-28-2000||09:53 PM||||I replaced my drivers side mirror earlier this year. I just got one from the local salvage yard. All I did was slide a wide flat blade putty knife underneath the glass and worked it up and under.Got the glass off with no problem.Turned out, the factory glue was just silicone.Then just silicone it back on yours.||||reg||6
Z||000009||theogre||12-28-2000||11:23 PM||||There's planty of cave notes on doors and windows..... could be fender or door. likely door.<P>the mirror glass is available at nearly any autoparts store. Usually in Motor Mite's HELP! package with other door stuff. Pep Boys and most other chains likely have it in stock for the drivers side.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||12-29-2000||09:12 PM||||I'll take a look at the door this weekend.  I'm not terribly worried about it since it isn't use much.  Just wanted to see how to fix it.  <P>I'll also look at Autozone tomorrow after work and see if they have the mirror glass.  If not, maybe they can order it for me.  Sounds easy enough to fix.  <P>Now on to the stereo.  I'm not too worried (not). <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
